                    <div class="bg-slate-900 p-5 rounded-xl border border-slate-800 space-y-2">
                        <span class="text-xs font-mono text-emerald-400">VELOCITY OPTIMIZATION FORMULA</span>
                        <div class="p-3 bg-slate-950 rounded font-mono text-cyan-300 text-sm text-center my-2">
                            V<sub>opt</sub> = min( V<sub>limit</sub> , &radic;(2 &middot; a<sub>eco</sub> &middot; d<sub>target</sub>) )
                        </div>
                        <p class="text-xs text-slate-400">Where $a_{\text{eco}} \approx 1.0 - 1.2\text{ m/s}^2$. Ensures deceleration remains smoothly distributed, keeping engine in peak efficiency island (2,000 - 2,500 RPM).</p>
                    </div>

                    <div class="bg-slate-900 p-5 rounded-xl border border-slate-800 space-y-2">
                        <span class="text-xs font-mono text-amber-400">TERRAIN POWER DEMAND FORMULA</span>
                        <div class="p-3 bg-slate-950 rounded font-mono text-amber-300 text-xs text-center my-2">
                            P<sub>demand</sub> = ( m g sin&theta; + m a + C<sub>r</sub> m g cos&theta; + &frac12; &rho; A C<sub>d</sub> V<sup>2</sup> ) &middot; V
                        </div>
                        <p class="text-xs text-slate-400">On incline ($\theta > 0$), velocity bleeds off naturally to prevent high-RPM NOx spikes. On decline ($\theta < 0$), DFCO zero-fuel coasting is activated.</p>
                    </div>
                </div>
